      "id": "MBF-01",
      "title": "Two sources of denominators in a primitive Bernoulli factor",
      "statement": "For k≥2, f positive and f|N, multiplication by f clears the negative exponent of f in the Bernoulli-polynomial expansion; the product of primes through k+1 clears the ordinary Bernoulli denominators. Character summation and multiplication by N/f give the integral factor N·primorial(k+1)·B_{k,χ*}.",
